login":"pedrofernandss","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgyOTYxMDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pedrofernandss/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pedrofernandss/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pedrofernandss/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pedrofernandss/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pedrofernandss/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pedrofernandss","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pedrofernandss/law-in-voice/commits/2bf4678e4422669bd03776f44d8459185b3188af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T20:52:03Z","email":"pedrofernandes.olv@gmail.com","name":"Pedro Fernandes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T20:52:03Z","email":"pedrofernandes.olv@gmail.com","name":"Pedro Fernandes"},"message":"fix: preserve full request path when proxying /api/ to the backend\n\nproxy_pass''s target used a variable ($backend_upstream, needed for the\nlazy DNS resolution added earlier so the container can boot without a\nresolvable \"backend\" host). nginx disables its usual automatic prefix\nreplacement when proxy_pass contains a variable — instead of rewriting\n\"/api/convert\" to \"backend:8000/api/convert\", it was forwarding every\nrequest as the literal \"/api/\" from the proxy_pass string, dropping\neverything after it. POST /api/convert was reaching the backend as\nPOST /api/ (404).\n\nUse $request_uri instead of a hardcoded \"/api/\" suffix so the original\npath (and query string) passes through untouched. Verified end-to-end\nagainst a throwaway backend on a shared Docker network: the backend now\nreceives \"/api/convert\" instead of \"/api/\".","tree":{"sha":"43d16aa31fa5482b33562abfa099b11dbea4e8c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pedrofernandss/law-in-voice/git/trees/43d16aa31fa5482b33562abfa099b11dbea4e8c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/