ns_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binaryjack/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/binaryjack","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/binaryjack/synetics.dev/commits/ddb94febef2b291678aa94bd7909944632b81eb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-19T09:19:42Z","email":"pianatadeo@hotmail.com","name":"BinaryJack"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-19T09:19:42Z","email":"pianatadeo@hotmail.com","name":"BinaryJack"},"message":"fix(lifecycle): connect onCleanup/onMount to ._stack via context-bus\n\nProblem: lifecycle-hooks.ts used currentElement (never set) so onCleanup\nalways warned and silently no-oped - intervals leaked on unmount.\n\nSolution:\n- src/lifecycle/context-bus.ts (new): zero-dep slot stack\n  pushContext()/popContext()/registerCallback() - no imports from registry\n- src/lifecycle/lifecycle-hooks.ts: register via registerCallback() instead\n  of checking currentElement\n- src/registry/core/prototype/execute.ts: pushContext() before factory,\n  popContext() after; attach cleanup fns to _nodes as WireDisposers so\n  disposeElement() runs them; call mount fns immediately after creation\n\nNo circular imports: execute -> context-bus (zero deps)\n                     lifecycle-hooks -> context-bus (zero deps)","tree":{"sha":"201ff02357d398d5eeb6df00e1f514a085ae131e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/binaryjack/synetics.dev/git/trees/201ff02357d398d5eeb6df00e1f514a085ae131e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/binaryjack/synetics.dev/git/commits/ddb94febef2b291678aa94bd7909944632b81eb6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1678563?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binaryjack/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binaryjack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/binaryjack/following{/o