eb-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/b44e28579fd44ce0a5b07370c437dda357b90ecb","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKGI0NGUyODU3OWZkNDRjZTBhNWIwNzM3MGM0MzdkZGEzNTdiOTBlY2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/3444f7c5a5ead9a49c8898f97628f8e4b35ba1ad","sha":"3444f7c5a5ead9a49c8898f97628f8e4b35ba1ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/3444f7c5a5ead9a49c8898f97628f8e4b35ba1ad"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/bbe85aea037c4927b97833e8e009987020cdfa9d","sha":"bbe85aea037c4927b97833e8e009987020cdfa9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/bbe85aea037c4927b97833e8e009987020cdfa9d"}],"sha":"b44e28579fd44ce0a5b07370c437dda357b90ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/b44e28579fd44ce0a5b07370c437dda357b90ecb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/563efc6ba339d124753ec891b3e6990c1a26ddd6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:59:59Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:59:59Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(shell): keep the application on screen while a page loads, and rank the nav\n\nTwo things the shell was doing to itself.\n\nRouteLoadingFallback was a spinner on an empty min-h-screen, and the Suspense\nboundary sat above the whole route tree - so every navigation to a lazily loaded\npage unmounted the header and the navigation along with the content and rebuilt\nthem. Seven skeleton components exist and 39 screens use them; the loading\nlanguage was good everywhere except the moment you actually changed page. The\nshell now suspends its own outlet, so React reaches that boundary first and only\nthe content is drawn as absent. Verified by sampling every 40ms across a\nnavigation: the header and nav never unmount, and the content skeleton appears.\n\nThe navigation rendered all fourteen items at one weight across three rows, a\nthird of the window, so Documents read exactly like Admin Ops. Every route\nalready declares which section it belongs to and getSectionLabel has been\nwaiting to be used - the primary section now sits at full weight with its icons\nand the rest keeps its place, quieter and smaller. Nothing is hidden and no menu\nwas added. 33% of the viewport down to 26%.\n\nThe split follows what routes.ts declares, not a judgement of mine: Reviews is\n`management` there, so it sits in the second row. Moving it is one word.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f309bbb2a323df2f7b7057b52bf421fbf3cf082","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/9f309bbb2a323df2f7b7057b52bf421fbf3cf082"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/563efc6ba339d124753ec891b3e6990c1a26ddd6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/563efc6ba339d124753ec891b3e6990c1a26ddd6","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDU2M2VmYzZiYTMzOWQxMjQ3NTNlYzg5MWIzZTY5OTBjMWEyNmRkZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/3444f7c5a5ead9a49c8898f97628f8e4b35ba1ad","sha":"3444f7c5a5ead9a49c8898f97628f8e4b35ba1ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/3444f7c5a5ead9a49c8898f97628f8e4b35ba1ad"}],"sha":"563efc6ba339d124753ec891b3e6990c1a26ddd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/563efc6ba339d124753ec891b3e6990c1a26ddd6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/bbe85aea037c4927b97833e8e009987020cdfa9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:24:12Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T22:24:41Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(conversion): stop dropping the images a PDF carries\n\nMeasured on a twenty-page Intel guide with 42 raster images, 1.44 MB of the\nfile''s 1.9 MB: two images survived the PDF to HTML path and twenty-one warnings\nread \"failed to embed image: \" with nothing after the colon.\n\npython-docx sniffs an image stream for a header it recognises. PyMuPDF hands\nback the stream exactly as the PDF stores it, which for these JPEGs has none, so\npython-docx raised UnrecognizedImageError - an exception that stringifies to\nnothing, which is how forty missing images stayed invisible for as long as they\ndid. The warning now uses !r, so a silent exception still names itself.\n\nRendering through a pixmap produces a header every time: 42 of 42 embed. Doing\nonly that costs 8.97 MB where the PDF carried 1.44 MB, because a pixmap written\nas PNG is lossless and these are screenshots. Two things bring it back:\n\n  - anything without real transparency is written as JPEG at quality 85\n  - a soft mask is only honoured when it actually hides something. 36 of the 42\n    images here carry a mask and not one of them hides a pixel; attaching it\n    anyway adds an alpha channel, which forces PNG. This alone was 8.86 MB\n    against 2.06 MB of HTML.\n\nNothing is downscaled. These are screenshots of interfaces and the text inside\nthem is why the page is being read; capping the long edge at 1600px saves 24%\nwhere the JPEG decision already saved 82%. Instead a document whose images pass\n6 MB says so, through the warning channel the preview already surfaces.\n\nResult on the same document: 2 images -> 23, warnings 21 -> 0, HTML 0.29 MB ->\n2.06 MB, conversion time unchanged at 5.1s.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cf365278ee4e39b15dc972168197a944b635e23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/3cf365278ee4e39b15dc972168197a944b635e23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/bbe85aea037c4927b97833e8e009987020cdfa9d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEst