s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/7d608fe2c0e62f02ccbf001a643cfc5bcee46b16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:22:14Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:22:14Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(ui): give every document status one name and one explanation\n\nThe internal table was a chain of ternaries that named only `active` and\n`approved` and let the rest fall through to the raw enum, so `draft` appeared\nlowercase beside `Published` in the same table and `pending_review` would have\nshown its underscore. The public pages ran a generic title-caser, which reads\n`active` as \"Active\" - correct English, and a different word from the one the\ninternal screens use for the same state.\n\nOne map now: Draft, In Review, Approved, Published, Archived, each with the tone\nand a description. `PUBLISHED` and `ACTIVE` are the same value in the backend\nenum, so \"Published\" is its one name. `approved` keeps its name and gains the\nsentence a pill cannot hold - a reviewer accepted it, and it is not yet visible\nto customers - which is the distinction that was unclear.\n\nThe visibility control keeps its place in the row. It opens a confirmation that\ncaptures a reason, so it is not the unguarded edit it looked like; what it was\nis a 160x39 form control beside a 53x26 pill, in a language nothing else in the\nrow spoke. Now 95x28 and shaped like the row''s other tokens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2c3072fc7423fb01c5d0dc1cd21a3a7e1c3b3562","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/2c3072fc7423fb01c5d0dc1cd21a3a7e1c3b3562"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/7d608fe2c0e62f02ccbf001a643cfc5bcee46b16","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/7d608fe2c0e62f02ccbf001a643cfc5bcee46b16","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDdkNjA4ZmUyYzBlNjJmMDJjY2JmMDAxYTY0M2NmYzViY2VlNDZiMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852","sha":"4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852"}],"sha":"7d608fe2c0e62f02ccbf001a643cfc5bcee46b16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/7d608fe2c0e62f02ccbf001a643cfc5bcee46b16"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:07:13Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T21:07:13Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(ui): show a document''s date the same way on every screen\n\nThere were three formats. `toLocaleDateString()` with no arguments follows the\n*browser''s* locale, so the same document read 8/23/2026 for one viewer and\n23.8.2026 for another - 19 of the 22 call sites did that. The rest pinned\n''en-US'' with either month: ''short'' (Mar 20, 2026) or month: ''long'' (March 20,\n2026). ViewerDocumentPage carried two of them at once.\n\nformatDocumentDate now sits beside the module that already owns the user''s\nlocale and timezone preferences, and every document surface - internal list,\nviewer, customer portal, public catalogue, changelog - goes through it. The\nformat follows the internal list, as asked, and the locale is the user''s own\nrather than whichever browser they happened to open.\n\nLeft alone: MyFeedbackPage renders a date *and* a time, which a document date\nnever does. The remaining call sites are admin and notification surfaces, not\ndocument identity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"190db0bd51f95e27bbe12a8408e10dd261cded07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/190db0bd51f95e27bbe12a8408e10dd261cded07"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDRiZDYyYjFkNzA5ODU5OWI2OTcyYTk2Y2M0ODBiOTQ1OTA5Yjk4NTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee","sha":"a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee"}],"sha":"4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/4bd62b1d7098599b6972a96cc480b945909b9852"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T20:32:19Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T20:32:19Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(ui): stop admin table cells collapsing below the width of a word\n\n.admin-table-cell carried overflow-wrap: anywhere, which drops a cell''s\nmin-content width to a single character. A squeezed table then shaved the\ndocument column instead of letting the shell scroll, which it was already\nwilling to do. At a 700px viewport the title column fell to 115px and\n\"709759-005 (2)\" broke two characters per line: the title box was 842px tall\nand the row 871px - taller than the viewport, for one document.\n\nSame failure the release-note tables had, same fix: break-word still breaks a\ntoken that genuinely cannot fit but leaves the intrinsic width alone. Measured\nat the same 700px: title column 381px, title box 118px, tallest row 147px, and\nthe shell still scrolls horizontally.\n\nA row-header cell is a <th>, which the browser centres by default, so the\ndocument''s identity block sat centred while every other column was left-aligned.\n\nBoth fixes are on the shared class, so the nine admin tables get them together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c90dd54e5eb4078b77e66e3e40375d8652fb5ea0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/c90dd54e5eb4078b77e66e3e40375d8652fb5ea0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKGE2ZmVhZWI2OTEyYWFlMTA4MzMxNDJmYmFlNzVkY2Q2MzIxZjdkZWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/6ac658bcefafa8417c6aab73e388e240abd2af1c","sha":"6ac658bcefafa8417c6aab73e388e240abd2af1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/6ac658bcefafa8417c6aab73e388e240abd2af1c"}],"sha":"a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/a6feaeb6912aae10833142fbae75dcd6321f7dee"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/6ac658bcefafa8417c6aab73e388e240abd2af1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T18:57:59Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T18:57:59Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(ui): raise contrast to the level the type sizes call for\n\nIn dark mode the application''s own name was slate-900 on a near-black header:\n1.13:1. The eyebrow above it, the three summary cards on the documents page and\ntwo filter dropdowns had no dark variant either, so they stayed lit on a dark\npage. Giving the cards a dark surface then hid the values inside them, which had\nnever needed a variant while the card was white - they have one now.\n\nThe row actions are 12px uppercase, where 4.5:1 applies. Archive measured\n3.02:1, edit and delete 4.45:1. Moved to the -700 shades, with dark variants.\nSecondary text at slate-400 measured 2.43:1; slate-500 reads the same and\npasses.\n\nMeasured after, both themes: app name 14.22 light / 18.41 dark, edit 5.46 /\n10.06, archive 4.76 / 13.99, delete 5.96 / 10.67, secondary text 4.51 / 7.87,\nand no light surface left on a dark page.\n\nOnly the internal shell implements dark mode - PublicLayout and CustomerLayout\ncarry no dark variants and no theme toggle, and their header is a light brand\nband by construction. Dark variants added there would be white on light blue, so\nthey are deliberately left out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de801ac20f1de3b98b938dd757c5b1b7437c58b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/de801ac20f1de3b98b938dd757c5b1b7437c58b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_pr