ab86c0a7f39c5f2dba705b6dd144d","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKGMzYTVjNDcwNWUyYWI4NmMwYTdmMzljNWYyZGJhNzA1YjZkZDE0NGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/e0726de0605acea56ed46e953cbb306d06b905cf","sha":"e0726de0605acea56ed46e953cbb306d06b905cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/e0726de0605acea56ed46e953cbb306d06b905cf"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4","sha":"5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4"}],"sha":"c3a5c4705e2ab86c0a7f39c5f2dba705b6dd144d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/c3a5c4705e2ab86c0a7f39c5f2dba705b6dd144d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:13:51Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T08:13:51Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"docs: add CLAUDE.md and clear the closed audits out of the tree\n\nNothing in the repository told a new contributor how to work in it, so the same\nfew traps cost time repeatedly: backend/venv holds 65 of 119 pinned packages and\nits gaps fail silently rather than loudly - without fonttools a faithful PDF\nrender degrades to a serif fallback that looks like a bug and is not - uvicorn\nruns without --reload so edited files are visible but not loaded, ruff lives in\nthe venv the pre-push hook cannot see, and 51 backend tests fail on a clean\ncheckout for reasons that have nothing to do with any change under review.\n\nCLAUDE.md records those, the baseline to measure against, and the parts of the\nconversion architecture that took real investigation: that DOCX declares its\nstructure completely while a PDF barely does, that heading numbers exist only in\nthe generated contents page because Word renders them from the numbering\ndefinition, that layout is discarded early on the PDF path, and that pdf_layout\nand docx_structure are written and tested but wired to nothing.\n\nThe ten audits and execution plans removed here all declare themselves closed,\ncompleted or superseded, and describe work finished in March. They are noise to\nanyone reading the tree now and remain in history. REMEDIATION_PLAN.md stays: it\nstill carries 201 unchecked items, and its reference to the audit it derives\nfrom now points at the commit that holds it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"079029fee3b409e9f312726bb5d6e9baeef8bb84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/079029fee3b409e9f312726bb5d6e9baeef8bb84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDVlMWQ4MmExMWJlMzc4OTcxOGM0Y2U2Y2QyNDhiMGNjNjQ4NjRiYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420","sha":"cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420"}],"sha":"5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/5e1d82a11be3789718c4ce6cd248b0cc64864bc4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T21:40:48Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T21:40:48Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(reviews): stop the contents page and deleted documents polluting reviews\n\nAdding one section to a document produced a review reading \"1 added, 158\nremoved\". Running the real diff over the two stored versions showed what those\n158 were:\n\n  previous sections: 316   current sections: 159\n  prev anchors: [''page-10'', ''page-10'', ''page-11'', ...]\n  summary: unchanged 158, modified 0, added 1, removed 158\n\nThe 158 real headings matched perfectly. The removals were the *printed contents\npage*: every line of it became a body paragraph, and processHtmlIntoSections\nturns each into a phantom section anchored to a page number instead of a\nheading. Regenerating that page therefore reads as 158 deletions and buries the\none change the author made.\n\nWord''s contents page is navigation, not content, and it is already served\nseparately as the document''s own table of contents with real pages and stable\nanchors. Paragraphs styled \"toc 1\"..\"toc 9\" are no longer emitted into the body.\nOn the release notes that removes exactly 158 paragraphs, 4133 to 3975, leaving\nthe 158 headings and 127 tables untouched.\n\nSeparately, the review listings joined Document but never excluded deleted ones,\nso deleting a document left its open reviews in the queue permanently - two of\nthem were sitting there. Both listings now require the document to be live.\n\nBackend 51 failures before and after, all pre-existing, 1726 passing; frontend\n111 files and 432 tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1103c9757aab33fdb0022daa6709ae6760369f6b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/1103c9757aab33fdb0022daa6709ae6760369f6b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKGNmZjVjMjZkZGQzNDhlZWRkNDU5OGFiOGNiNTRmYWMzMWNiOWQ0MjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf","sha":"8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf"}],"sha":"cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/cff5c26ddd348eedd4598ab8cb54fac31cb9d420"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:53:46Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T09:53:46Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(versions): keep a version''s contents when it is created by an edit\n\nContents were built only on upload. Every other way a version comes into being -\nediting a section, editing the document, patching content - produced a row with\ntoc_json null, so the contents panel emptied after any edit and, worse, a review\ncompared a baseline holding 158 entries against a candidate holding none and\nreported all 158 as removed. On a document where one section had been touched,\nthe reviewer was shown 158 deletions.\n\nAn edit yields HTML, never the original file, so the contents cannot be read\nfrom a DOCX contents page again. Carrying the previous list forward unchanged\nwould be wrong the moment a heading is added, renamed or removed; recomputing\nfrom scratch would discard the page numbers, which HTML never holds. So the\nheadings come from the new HTML and the pages are carried across from the\nprevious entries, matched on the anchor id both share.\n\nA renamed heading keeps its number. The number lives only in the old title -\nWord renders it from the numbering definition and never writes it into the text -\nand an editor who renames \"Release Kit Summary\" to \"Release Kit Summary+draft\"\nstill means section 1.\n\nChecked against the document that exposed this: 158 entries derived, 158 anchors\nmatched, 158 pages carried, and 157 of 158 entries identical to the baseline -\nthe one difference being the section actually edited.\n\nPublishing only sets flags and audience snapshots, so content and contents both\nsurvive approval untouched. The one place that rewrites content in place, the\nversion PATCH, now rebuilds the contents alongside it.\n\nBackend 51 failures before and after, all pre-existing, 1725 passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"263ecbb964ddd7c1b6ebe9b0487fc71f04c2d54d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/263ecbb964ddd7c1b6ebe9b0487fc71f04c2d54d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDhkMTllNmM1ZGJlZDVjZjcwYmQxNDA4OTQ3OGYzYjI5NzY4MDI0YmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce","sha":"84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce"}],"sha":"8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/8d19e6c5dbed5cf70bd14089478f3b29768024bf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:45:18Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T15:45:18Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(documents): serve the stored contents and stop rendering field codes\n\nThree defects found by opening a converted release-notes document and reading\nthe screen rather than the counts.\n\nThe contents panel still listed scraped headings. _serialize_version builds an\nexplicit dict, and toc_json was not in it, so every version the service returned\ncarried an empty list however correctly it had been stored - the direct model\nvalidation returned 158 entries while the listing returned none.\n\nThe body opened with raw Word field instructions:\n\n  TOC \\o \"3-4\" \\h \\z \\t \"Heading 1,1,...\" 1 Release Kit Summary PAGEREF _Toc237367833 \\h 10\n\nw:instrText is a field *instruction*, never text a reader should see; a field''s\nvisible result is carried by the w:t runs that follow it. The extractor emitted\nboth, so 158 PAGEREF codes and the TOC switch string rendered as content. Only\nw:t is emitted now, and the contents page reads \"1 Release Kit Summary 10\".\nHeadings and tables are unchanged at 158 and 127.\n\nThe reading font was ''IBM Plex Serif'', which suits prose but misrepresents\ndocuments set in Verdana or Arial and reads poorly at the density of a\nspecification table. The stack is now sans and driven by a custom property, so a\nper-document override has somewhere to attach.\n\nBackend 51 failures before and after, all pre-existing, 1717 passing; frontend\n432 tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"da7be713b2fdca8547edc8b536f14b0ddf8a3f84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/da7be713b2fdca8547edc8b536f14b0ddf8a3f84"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDg0Y2M0M2U0ODUzNDhiODBhNTVhMTJmMTQ3ZTI1ZWYyNGVjNTExY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e","sha":"7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e"}],"sha":"84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/84cc43e485348b80a55a12f147e25ef24ec511ce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:30:24Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:30:24Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"feat(documents): store each version''s contents beside its HTML\n\nThe contents panel built its entries by sanitizing the stored HTML in the browser\nand scraping headings back out of the DOM. That can recover titles, but never\npage numbers, because nothing in a converted document holds them: the Current\nversion view therefore showed sections with no pages at all, and the active\nsection could not be tracked by page.\n\nThe structure is known at conversion time and is thrown away immediately after.\nconvert_document_to_html returns a string, so version_toc reads the structure\nfrom the same bytes the HTML came from - a DOCX states its contents outright,\na PDF states an outline - and the result is stored in versions.toc_json next to\nthe content it describes. Documents that declare nothing store nothing and keep\nthe previous behaviour.\n\nVersionResponse serves the stored entries as toc_items, parsing the JSON in a\nbefore-validator so a null or malformed column yields an empty list rather than\na failed response. The preview prefers those entries over scraped headings, so\nthe panel shows pages 10..109 with each title carrying its own numbering, and\nevery entry points at a heading id.\n\nVersionResponse.model_rebuild() moved below AttachmentOutlineItem, which it now\nreferences; leaving it above left the forward reference unresolved and stopped\nthe app importing.\n\nVerified against the full suites: backend 51 failures before and after, all\npre-existing, with 1717 passing; frontend 111 files and 432 tests passing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d02411c1aabf8796f8c88a0b49e3a8ffb40355e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/d02411c1aabf8796f8c88a0b49e3a8ffb40355e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDdmNmFlNTE4MGMyNzE2ZTFhZTZhNDdlMjNjMDE4YzA4M2MxMTI1MWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae","sha":"835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae"}],"sha":"7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/7f6ae5180c2716e1ae6a47e23c018c083c11251e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:30:09Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:30:09Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"chore(api): refresh the OpenAPI snapshot that had drifted from the backend\n\nbackend/openapi.contract.json is regenerated from a running backend, so it only\nmoves when someone runs refresh:api-contracts. Several endpoints had been added\nwithout that step and were missing from it: the attachment fidelity view, the\ndocument export route, portal comment endpoints, review ownership rules and\nreviewer candidates, and comment reopen.\n\ngenerate:api-contracts:check compares the generated frontend contracts against\nthis snapshot rather than against the live API, so the drift produced no failure\nand simply accumulated. Committed on its own so the catch-up is separable from\nthe change that prompted it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"afca5c44ce10c51a9629d41fba0495b927ceb17e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/afca5c44ce10c51a9629d41fba0495b927ceb17e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDgzNWJkNTk2OTEwYTVmMmJlMTUzYWVkYTU3MTI3NzE2MTIwOWI1YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68","sha":"ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68"}],"sha":"835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/835bd596910a5f2be153aeda571277161209b5ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:06:54Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:06:54Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"fix(conversion): take TOC page numbers from the document, not from heading order\n\nreader_artifact numbered contents entries like this:\n\n    page_number = getattr(heading, \"slide_number\", None) or (index + 1)\n\nslide_number belongs to PPTX. For DOCX it is always None, so every entry fell\nthrough to its own ordinal: the first heading was labelled page 1, the\nfifty-seventh page 57. Measured against the Intel release notes, 156 of 158\nentries carried a page the document never had, and the contents ran to \"page\n158\" in a document 109 pages long. That is the contents panel disagreeing with\nthe document it describes.\n\nThe page numbers were never missing. Word writes a contents page whose lines\ncarry number, title and page as tab-separated fields, and DocxExtractor holds\nthe bytes that contain it, so it is read there and attached to the extraction\nresult. Entries now report pages 10..109, each title carries the numbering the\nheadings themselves do not hold, and every one of the 158 anchors resolves to a\nheading id in the rendered HTML - making navigation a direct lookup rather than\na text search.\n\ndocument_toc builds the same shape for PDFs, where the outline leads and\ndetected headings fill in below it, so both formats produce one TOC vocabulary.\nOutput stays within AttachmentOutlineItem, so the response contract is unchanged\nand documents that declare nothing still fall back to the old ordinal.\n\nVerified against the full backend suite: 51 failures before the change and 51\nafter, all pre-existing and environmental, with 7 new tests added.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6bcb9fe3ab749fbd94eb760de0d98c3d86d1772f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/6bcb9fe3ab749fbd94eb760de0d98c3d86d1772f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKGZmMjI0NGZmNGMwZDViYThmNTYxMGMxMDgxNmNlZjFmN2U4YWJkNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03","sha":"59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03"}],"sha":"ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/ff2244ff4c0d5ba8f5610c10816cef1f7e8abd68"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T11:26:11Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T11:26:11Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"feat(conversion): read the structure DOCX declares about itself\n\nThe PDF path needed a layout model because a PDF states almost nothing about its\nown structure. DOCX is the mirror image: it has no coordinates and no page\nboundaries to recover, but it declares its structure completely. On the Intel\nrelease-notes template the declaration is exact at every depth - 11/54/63/30\nheading paragraphs against 11/54/63/30 contents entries - so guessing is not\nmerely unnecessary, it is worse than reading.\n\nTwo properties make the contents page the authority rather than the headings:\n\n- Heading paragraphs do not contain their numbers. Word renders those from the\n  numbering definition, so paragraph.text gives \"Release Kit Summary\" and never\n  \"1 Release Kit Summary\". The literal numbering survives only in the contents\n  entries, which carry number, title and page as tab-separated fields.\n- Those entries are ordinary body paragraphs. Left in the content they render as\n  a wall of dotted leaders, which is what the frontend currently tries to strip\n  back out heuristically. Lifting them into the structure removes the guess.\n\nEntries are matched forward through the headings, so titles that repeat under\nseveral chapters - which these templates do freely - bind to successive headings\ninstead of collapsing onto the first.\n\nThe ids are generated exactly as DocxExtractor generates its heading anchors, and\nthis was verified against the real document rather than assumed: 158 ids in the\nrendered HTML, 158 nodes, identical and in the same order, with all 158 contents\nentries resolving to an element. That makes navigation a direct\nentry -> id -> element lookup with no text search.\n\nNot wired to anything yet; the DOCX render path is untouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3f753a4e5b022e1eb543355649b037a99c23310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/d3f753a4e5b022e1eb543355649b037a99c23310"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03","node_id":"C_kwDOQ9kaMNoAKDU5ZDQ5YjBhY2FmYmMzNmUwNmU3ZDRjYmJkYjQyOGNhZWRlYzRmMDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Yogevso/finale_project/commit/24e645aa8be3077b6f97baf27e9766578a724c76","sha":"24e645aa8be3077b6f97baf27e9766578a724c76","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/24e645aa8be3077b6f97baf27e9766578a724c76"}],"sha":"59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/59d49b0acafbc36e06e7d4cbbdb428caedec4f03"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_kgDOCpSGeg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/commits/24e645aa8be3077b6f97baf27e9766578a724c76/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T11:19:01Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T11:19:01Z","email":"ronqik054@gmail.com","name":"Ron Estrin"},"message":"feat(conversion): extract PDFs into a layout-preserving document model\n\nconvert_pdf_to_docx reads span coordinates, sorts blocks by them and then drops\nthem. Everything downstream - the reader HTML, the section list, the table of\ncontents - is therefore reconstructed from a flow document that no longer knows\nwhat sat where, on which page, in what type. No amount of work in the extractor,\nthe renderer or the editor can recover that; the information is gone two layers\nearlier.\n\nThis adds the parallel path that keeps it. LayoutDocument carries pages with\ntheir real dimensions and nodes that hold semantic fields (type, level, number,\ntext) and layout fields (page, bbox, font family/size/weight, spans) on the same\nobject, so one node can serve editing, navigation, the TOC and rendering.\n\nThree behaviours come from measuring the Intel GCC user guide rather than from\nassumption:\n\n- A numbered heading is emitted as two lines on one baseline, the number far to\n  the left of the title. Joining spans without regard to their x-gap yields\n  \"2Key Known Issues\", and a first pass over the whole document found zero\n  numbering patterns as a result. Lines sharing a baseline are merged and joined\n  gap-aware, which recovers the numbering.\n- The running header names the current chapter, so its text changes every few\n  pages and repeated-text detection never sees it. It is matched on font\n  signature and vertical position instead, with x excluded because two-sided\n  layouts alternate it between margins. It then maps every page to the section\n  that owns it. Only the outermost repeated line counts, so a table header row\n  continued across pages stays content.\n- A heading is a line set entirely in heading type. An inline \"Note:\" run is\n  10pt bold above 9pt body and passes any size-or-weight test, but the body\n  continues on its line, so requiring uniformity rules it out without a rule\n  about the word.\n\nWhere the PDF ships an outline it is authoritative: it sets the levels it covers\nand the rest are shifted below it. On the guide this yields 4 headings matching\n4 of 4 outline entries, with full text coverage against raw extraction.\n\nNothing is wired to this yet; convert_pdf_to_docx and the DOCX path are\nuntouched.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d3c84654f70f27d06edc0c6e2ae677658d27745f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/trees/d3c84654f70f27d06edc0c6e2ae677658d27745f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Yogevso/finale_project/git/commits/24e645aa8be3077b6f97baf27e9766578a724c76","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177505914?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RonEstrin12/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/RonEstrin12","id":177505914,"login":"RonEstrin12","node_id":"U_k